<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pingjin campaign</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1948–1949</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-civil-war">Chinese Civil War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pingjin campaign was the last of the three great campaigns of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-civil-war">Chinese Civil War</a>, fought around Beiping (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>) and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tianjin">Tianjin</a> from November 1948 to January 1949. Communist forces under Lin Biao and Nie Rongzhen stormed Tianjin, and the Nationalist commander Fu Zuoyi surrendered Beiping without a fight, leaving northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in Communist hands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pingjin-campaign.jpg" alt="Pingjin campaign" width="320" height="251" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Aukingluntom at Chinese Wikipedia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PLA_Enters_Peking.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
